{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: read the item and note from the token stream too",
  "description": "The measurement at the front of a line (amount, range, size, unit, package) is now read by the grammar in ramekin-core/src/ingredient_parser/measure.rs over the tokens from tokens.rs. \
Everything after it in parse_ingredient (mod.rs, Steps 4.4a onward) is still a chain of string passes: \"plus\" compounds, \"or\" alternatives and borrowing the food across \"or\", trailing comma notes, \"to taste\" guidance, mixing instructions, brand vs. food Title Case, leading quality words. \
Each pass re-finds its boundaries with find(\" or \") / find(\",\") on the remaining string, and fixes keep colliding (an \"or\" inside a note, a comma inside a parenthetical, a brand before \"or\"). \
Next phase of p3-ingredient-parser-rewrite: split the rest of the line into token segments at top-level commas, \"or\", \"plus\"/\"+\" and \"/\" once, then classify the segments (alternative measurement, item, note, guidance). \
Pin behavior with the pipeline fixtures as before, rerun make pipeline, and name every data/ diff. \
Known wrong today: \"Slightly heaped 1/8, 1/4 or 1/2 teaspoon active dry yeast\" reads the item as \"1/4\"; a list of alternative amounts should parse as alternatives of one unit.",
